  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthened capacity of member States to ratify and apply international labour standards and to fulfil their reporting obligations</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This intervention aims to strengthen the capacity of Afghanistan&#x2019;s labour market institutions to apply and report on international labour standards (ILS) in line with the country&#x2019;s obligations as an ILO Member State. ILO works to enhance constituents institutional and technical capacity to align labour policies and legislation with ILS and fulfil reporting requirements in a timely and effective manner.  The programme supports consultations on fundamental conventions and improves the application of previously ratified standards. It also builds the capacities of constituents to coordinate and contribute meaningfully to reporting processes, engage with supervisory mechanisms, and implement recommendations, including those linked to the Conference Committee on the Application of Standards and the Committee on Freedom of Association. In a context characterized by political instability, weak governance structures, restricted civic participation, and limited oversight mechanisms, this intervention promotes rule of law, social justice, and accountability through stronger normative frameworks. By reinforcing engagement and compliance with international standards, the initiative supports decent work and contributes to Afghanistan&#x2019;s broader development and recovery objectives. Ultimately, this programme ensures that Afghanistan is better equipped to meet its ILO obligations, improve labour governance, and uphold fundamental principles and rights at work.</narrative>
  </description>
